L"}],"symbolKind":"enum","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"identifier"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same MusicXML semantics.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hie